.TH LUFUS 1 "September 2026" "Lufus 0.2.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lufus \- create bootable USB media on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lufus
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Lufus
is an independent Linux fork of Rufus.  Its GTK interface and command-line
interface submit work to the same privilege-separated disk engine.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List eligible removable devices.
.TP
.B checksum
Calculate image checksums.
.TP
.B write
Write raw, Windows installer, Windows To Go, or persistent Linux media.
.TP
.B capture
Capture a device as raw, fixed VHD, or dynamic VHDX.
.TP
.B test-device
Run destructive F3 capacity and block testing.
.TP
.B download
Discover or download supported Microsoft Windows and UEFI Shell images.
.SH OPTIONS
Run
.B lufus COMMAND --help
for the options accepted by a specific command.  Destructive noninteractive
writes require
.BR --yes .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/lufus/copyright
Debian-format copyright and license record.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/lufus/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
Bundled-component licenses, revisions, and provenance.
.TP
.I /usr/share/lufus/sources/
Corresponding source for pinned bundled components.
.SH SAFETY
Writing or testing a device destroys its contents.  Verify the complete target
path and disconnect unrelated disks before creating silent-install media.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR 7z (1),
.BR wimlib-imagex (1),
.BR qemu-img (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Rufus by Pete Batard and contributors; Lufus Linux implementation by Open
Research Tools contributors.
